<title>NORWAY: FORECAST - UBN Q1 profits seen down.</title>
<headline>FORECAST - UBN Q1 profits seen down.</headline>
<dateline>OSLO 1997-04-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Union Bank of Norway, Norway's third biggest bank, is seen to book first-quarter operating profits of 346 million crowns, down from 401 million in the same year-ago period, according to a consensus forecast by six analysts polled by Reuters.</p>
<p>Five recommended to buy the share, while one said hold.</p>
<p>Shares in UBN, the country's largest savings bank, are known as primary capital certificates.</p>
<p>UBN, known in Norway as Sparebanken NOR, will present the first-quarter result at 0600 GMT on Tuesday.</p>
<p>					    Three months to March 31</p>
<p>				    (millions of crowns unless stated)</p>
<p>				     average   high    low	Q1 96</p>
<p> Net interest income	     648	690    610	 611</p>
<p> Non-interest op. income	 416	433    394	 333</p>
<p> Operating costs		   702	735    665	 662</p>
<p>Operating profit before</p>
<p> losses and writedowns	   362	388    342	 362</p>
<p> Operating profit		  346	388    321	 401</p>
<p> EPS Q1 (crowns)		  6,92     7,85   6,60	8,64</p>
<p> EPS 1997			  27,88    33,73  25,25</p>
<p> EPS 1998			  24,56    27,76  21,54</p>
<p> Dividend 1997 (crowns)	15,00    15,00  15,00</p>
<p>--Oslo newsroom, Alf Asklund +47 22 93 69 71</p>
